==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|xno}} and {{etyl|fro}} {{term|bailif}} (plural {{term|bailis}}), {{etyl|LL.}} *{{term||baiulivus}}. Compare Modern French {{term|bailli|lang=fr}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|bāʹ-lĭf}}, {{IPA|/ˈbeɪlɪf/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"beIlIf/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{legal}} A legal [[officer]] to whom some degree of [[authority]], care or [[jurisdiction]] is committed.
# {{British}} The [[steward]] or [[overseer]] of an [[estate]].

====Related terms====
* [[bailie]]
* [[bailiwick]]

